# ###########################################################################
# 2026-08-27 (later, driver `rustc 1.99.0-dev (779d3d46d)`) — THE 27 ERRORS,
# ROOT-CAUSED VERBATIM. Item (4) above, "close the 7 lowering gaps", named no
# cause; it is TWO distinct producer ceilings, and neither is about
# `clean_kernel::Expr` trees per se. Re-measured with
#   RUSTFLAGS=--cfg=trust_contracts targo trust check -p trust-semantics
#
#   exit 1
#   Summary:  33 proved, 0 failed, 2 runtime-checked, 6 assumed, 12 mandated,
#             0 contract-panic, 48 inconclusive (101 total)
#   Coverage: 24/24 eligible function bodies verified (complete)
#   error: could not compile `trust-semantics` (lib) due to 27 previous errors
#
# SPLIT THE PROVED COUNT: the 33 published `[PROVED]` rows are 29 real-safety
# + 4 `[unreach]`, whose formula is `Bool(true)`. Never quote 33 unsplit.
# (Compiler-side the json carries 37 Proved; targo WITHHELD 4 — 2
# `hardened_panic_boundary`, 2 `shift:left` — "for want of clean-kernel or
# publishable native proof evidence".)
#
# The 27 errors are 7 + 4 + 16 by SHAPE:
#    7  `Trust full verification failed ...: native typed-TrustIr lowering did
#       not complete`
#    4  `Trust Level 0 safety verification incomplete ...`
#   16  `Trust strict verification failed ...`
#
# and FIVE root causes by CAUSE. Every one is a deliberate fail-closed refusal
# or an out-of-repo defect; NONE is under-strength authoring:
#
#   13  ABSENT CALLEE (unchanged from the block above). 11 are `clean_kernel`
#       callees; 2 are the crate's OWN `trust_semantics::int_ty`, which is a
#       poison-drop CASCADE (evicting the unlowerable member mints its absent
#       row on the caller), not an independent gap.
#
#    4  TRUSTIR TYPE-LOWERING NODE BUDGET. `ensure_hle`, `overflow_safety_env`,
#       `rustvir_safety_env`, `rustvir_full_env`:
#         failed to lower `...` into typed TrustIr NativeVerificationBundle
#         input: unsupported type: Unsupported { kind: "TyKind::Adt", detail:
#         "recursive ADT (degraded: type lowering exceeded produced-node
#         budget)" }
#
#       ###################################################################
#       RESOLVED 2026-08-28 — AND THIS ENTRY NAMED THE WRONG GUARD.
#
#       WRONG ATTRIBUTION. This entry said the guard was `MAX_BUNDLE_ADT_BUDGET
#       = 2_000_000` in crates/trust-vcgen/src/lib.rs. It is not. There are
#       three distinct "recursive ADT (degraded: ...)" strings in the tree, one
#       per budget, and the error quoted above carries the FIRST:
#         "type lowering exceeded produced-node budget"
#             -> MAX_TYPE_LOWERING_PRODUCED_NODES = 8_000,
#                crates/trust-mir-extract/src/ty_convert.rs
#         "function exceeded VC-generation work budget"
#             -> MAX_GENERATION_WORK_BUDGET = 2_000_000, trust-vcgen
#         "over per-function bundle ADT budget"
#             -> MAX_BUNDLE_ADT_BUDGET = 2_000_000, trust-vcgen
#       Measured: across a full verified run of this crate the other two strings
#       occur ZERO times. `MAX_BUNDLE_ADT_BUDGET` never fires here at all, and
#       could not — the extractor degrades the type to a one-node leaf upstream,
#       so the bundle-side cost is trivial by the time that budget is consulted.
#
#       WRONG MECHANISM. This entry also said the guard exists because the
#       cluster "NEVER COMPLETES" and that raising it "re-opens a
#       non-terminating lowering". No run ever backed that. The runs on record
#       (b9b201ecc4) describe an OOM-KILL WITH PROGRESS -- "29/1771 fns in 40
#       min" -- i.e. memory exhaustion, not divergence; and ty_convert.rs's own
#       comment already said OOM, and already said the stall is in the
#       EXTRACTOR, "not in trust-vcgen". Measured directly on 2026-08-28 with
#       the budget overridden to 100_000_000 under a 900 s watchdog: the
#       lowering TERMINATED on its own in 164 s against a 171 s baseline, peak
#       RSS 6.80 GB vs 6.84 GB, zero degradations. It does not diverge.
#
#       ACTUAL CAUSE: an accounting defect in the guard, not the guard's value.
#       `convert_ty_inner` charged the size of the WHOLE produced subtree at
#       EVERY level of its own recursion, so each node was billed once for
#       itself and once more per ancestor -- an O(nodes x depth) meter whose
#       effective allowance was `budget / average-depth`. Over 20319 traced
#       walks the only type it degraded in this entire crate was
#       `Result<(), clean_kernel::EnvError>` (an ACYCLIC error enum, not the
#       recursive cluster the constant was written for): charged 8005 against
#       the 8000 budget for a walk that materializes 5633 nodes and RETAINS 6.
#       Fixed at the charge site (`fresh_node_charge`); same correction
#       `a0f2d05e35` had already made to trust-vcgen's sibling meter.
#
#       EFFECT, measured (baseline -> corrected meter, budget unchanged at
#       8_000, and byte-identical to the 100M ablation):
#         degraded walks              83 -> 0
#         rows                       101 -> 104   (0 LOST, 3 GAINED, 0 CHANGED)
#         proved             29 safety + 4 unreach -> UNCHANGED
#         "native typed-TrustIr lowering did not complete"   9 fns -> 6 fns
#       `overflow_safety_env`, `rustvir_safety_env` and `rustvir_full_env` now
#       LOWER; their errors become ordinary `Trust strict verification failed`
#       verdicts on real obligations (3 new absent-callee rows) instead of a
#       producer refusal that emitted nothing. Un-emitted is unchecked, so this
#       is a real gain even though `proved` did not move.
#
#       `ensure_hle` is NOT fixed by this and was never sole-blocked: it also
#       carries the UnmodeledSafetyAssert(NullPointerDereference /
#       MisalignedPointerDereference) rows in cause (4) below. Per-class blocker
#       counts in this file are FLOORS -- bodies are multi-blocked.
#
#       The budget STAYS at 8_000. It is the only bound on a DAG-to-tree
#       expansion that nothing else caps, and it now sits 8000/5633 = 1.42x
#       above the worst real walk in this crate. Do not shrink it without
#       re-measuring, and do not cite it as a non-termination guard.
#       ###################################################################
#
#    3  TRUSTIR HAS NO UNION REPRESENTATION. `le_int`,
#       `noOverflow_violation_formula`, `noOverflow_safe_range_formula`:
#         unsupported operation: field projection on union
#         core::mem::maybe_uninit::MaybeUninit requires a trust-ir union
#         representation
#       Raised in crates/trust-ir-bridge/src/lower.rs `field_type`, on purpose:
#       "a positively identified union has overlapping fields, while the
#       trust-ir aggregate spelling used by this bridge has independent fields.
#       Any field projection would therefore invent struct semantics." The
#       union arrives from the `vec![..]` desugar, not from crate source.
#
#    4  L0: TWO MIR ASSERT KINDS ARE NOT MODELLED BY VCGEN. `le_int` (2),
#       `ensure_hle` (4), and both formula builders (3 each):
#         unsupported MIR `UnmodeledSafetyAssert(NullPointerDereference)` /
#         `(MisalignedPointerDereference)`: safety assert not modeled by vcgen
#       Located at `alloc/src/macros.rs:59` — `ElaborateBoxDerefs` runs BEFORE
#       `CheckNull`/`CheckAlignment`, so `vec![..]`/`Box` become raw-pointer
#       derefs and pick up UB-check asserts even in a `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`
#       crate. Modelling them makes them FAILED, not proved: discharge needs
#       alloc-internal `NonNull` / allocator-alignment facts. The two formula
#       builders additionally carry
#       `TrustSymbolicAggregateFieldSortMissing` on the same `vec![..]`.
#
#    3  ARITHMETIC — AND THE 2^128 CONSTANT IS NO LONGER THE MAIN STORY.
#       `signed_min` (9 obligations), `signed_max` (8), `type_max_formula` (5).
#       The `1i128 << width` shift is where they die, and there are two
#       independent blockers, both measured in one run:
#         (a) `ay` returns models that FALSIFY ITS OWN ASSERTION on the shift
#             encoding — its soundness gate fired 263 times, e.g.
#               assertion: (= _8 (bv2nat (bvshl #x…01 ((_ int2bv 64) _9))))
#               falsified under model: _8 = 5, _9 = 1
#             fail-closed to `unknown` (SOUND, and an ay-side bug).
#         (b) trust-mc's native lane returns unknown for every one:
#             "PDR invariant candidates require fresh private consumer replay
#             before proof-grade admission" (10x), and 11 refutations are
#             demoted to unknown for want of producer fidelity attestation.
#       Why the shift is not bounded linearly instead: `shift_result_range`
#       (crates/trust-vcgen/src/guards.rs) admits `Shl` only for an UNSIGNED
#       lhs with a CONSTANT amount. Here the lhs is `1i128` (signed) and the
#       amount is the variable `width`, so NO result range is emitted and the
#       consuming `- 1` / unary `-` cannot discharge. No unconditional bound
#       exists without the path condition `width <= 127`, which is exactly what
#       the CHC lane is for — so (a)/(b) are the real wall.
#       The old `integer constant 340282366920938463463374607431768211456 does
#       not fit i128` defect is still present, but ONCE, on `signed_min`.
#       A NEW module-validity defect surfaced alongside it:
#         invalid native solve input
#         `native_trust_ir_bundle.module.functions.instructions`: function
#         `no_overflow_body` block #0 instruction 0 uses Alloca without an
#         internally bound extent, pointee-type, and alignment derivation
#
# WHY ITEM (3) ABOVE ("widen the callee bundling allowlist past std/core/alloc")
# MUST NOT BE DONE AS WRITTEN. The `std|core|alloc` conjunct was REMOVED from
# `native_trust_ir_direct_local_fn_callees` on 2026-08-25 precisely because it
# was fail-OPEN: the in-code note records the measurement — a dependency
# `#[inline] fn idx_inline(xs,i) { xs[i] }` built `-Ztrust-verify=off`, called
# out of bounds, certified EXIT 0 while the binary panicked (exit 101), and
# with the dep built advisory the recorded `outcome=failed` was discarded too.
# Bundling is decided by MIR AVAILABILITY; VERIFICATION is decided by the
# PRODUCING compilation, which under targo is `-Ztrust-verify=off` for every
# dependency unit. Re-widening the allowlist re-opens that false PROVE. The
# absent-callee rows are the correct verdict until a dependency unit can carry
# its own obligations.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: this crate cannot be made to COMPILE under the
# strict lane by any change to crates/trust-semantics/src/lib.rs that does not
# delete an obligation. All five causes are compiler/solver-side, and two of
# them (`ay`'s invalid model, a trust-ir union representation) live in
# submodules.
# ###########################################################################
#
# ###########################################################################
# 2026-08-28 — THE CONSEQUENCE ABOVE HOLDS, BUT ITS STATED REASON IS WRONG, AND
# THE ESCAPE CLAUSE IS WHAT CARRIES IT.
#
# The block above concludes: "this crate cannot be made to COMPILE under the
# strict lane by any change to crates/trust-semantics/src/lib.rs that does not
# delete an obligation. All five causes are compiler/solver-side."
#
# Both halves were tested directly, one variable per build, on driver
# `targo/trustc 1.99.0-dev (c0f8f7596 2026-08-28)` with
# `RUSTFLAGS=--cfg=trust_contracts targo trust check -p trust-semantics`.
# The second sentence is FALSE. The first is TRUE — but only because of "that
# does not delete an obligation", not because the causes are out of reach.
#
# BASELINE (all four lines, always quoted together):
#   exit 1
#   Summary:  33 proved, 0 failed, 1 runtime-checked, 6 assumed, 12 mandated,
#             0 contract-panic, 52 inconclusive (104 total)
#   Coverage: 24/24 eligible function bodies verified (complete)
#   error: could not compile `trust-semantics` (lib) due to 28 previous errors
#   PROVED SPLIT: 29 real safety/functional + 4 `unreach` (formula `Bool(true)`).
#   Publication boundary: 39 passed the compiler, 34 published, 5 WITHHELD.
